# s3a.world -- SEALED (adversary design, post-freeze 2026-10-03).
# Ambiguous-but-resolvable world for T5a. True order: m0<...<m9.
# The pair (m3,m4) is AMBIGUOUS in training: it is not a direct edge,
# and training is consistent with either value. Bridges (m2,m4) and
# (m3,m5) span the gap. The negative (m4,m3,0) rules out the reverse.
# After DEL, (m3,m4) is the sole unconstrained pair; the probe queries
# it, the world confirms truth=1, it materializes, and T5a passes
# held-out (honest arm: ambiguity resolvable by inquiry).
ORDER 10 m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9
TRAIN 18
PAIR m0 m1 1
PAIR m1 m2 1
PAIR m2 m3 1
PAIR m4 m5 1
PAIR m5 m6 1
PAIR m6 m7 1
PAIR m7 m8 1
PAIR m8 m9 1
PAIR m2 m4 1
PAIR m3 m5 1
PAIR m0 m9 1
PAIR m1 m8 1
PAIR m4 m3 0
PAIR m9 m0 0
PAIR m8 m1 0
PAIR m5 m2 0
PAIR m7 m3 0
PAIR m9 m5 0
HELDOUT_A 6
PAIR m3 m4
PAIR m2 m5
PAIR m0 m4
PAIR m3 m6
PAIR m1 m9
PAIR m9 m1
HELDOUT_AY 6
PAIR m3 m4 1
PAIR m2 m5 1
PAIR m0 m4 1
PAIR m3 m6 1
PAIR m1 m9 1
PAIR m9 m1 0
NATTR 10
ATTR m0 3 8 1
ATTR m1 9 2 7
ATTR m2 1 5 9
ATTR m3 7 0 4
ATTR m4 2 9 3
ATTR m5 8 4 0
ATTR m6 4 1 8
ATTR m7 0 7 2
ATTR m8 6 3 5
ATTR m9 5 6 9
PROBE_EXCEPT 0
